.\" wland(8) — NextBSD 802.11 management daemon.
.\"
.\" NextBSD-original. There is no upstream page to vendor: Apple's counterpart
.\" (wifid) is closed source and undocumented.
.\"
.Dd October 31, 2026
.Dt WLAND 8
.Os NextBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm wland
.Nd 802.11 management daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
owns 802.11 on NextBSD.
It is started by
.Xr launchd 8
as
.Ql org.nextbsd.wland
and is not intended to be run by hand.
Use
.Xr wlan 8
to talk to it.
.Pp
It exists because two things on the path from
.Dq Intel card
to
.Dq IP address
had no owner at all:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Sy Nothing created the VAP .
On FreeBSD an 802.11 driver does not present a usable interface \(em you must
clone a Virtual AP off the PHY, which
.Xr rc.conf 5
normally does with
.Ql wlans_iwlwifi0="wlan0" .
NextBSD has no
.Xr rc.conf 5
and no
.Pa /etc/rc.d ,
and never will:
.Xr launchd 8
is PID 1.
So
.Ql ifconfig wlan0 create wlandev iwlwifi0
had nobody to run it.
.Nm
does, natively
.Pq Dv SIOCIFCREATE2 ,
with a wildcard name so the kernel assigns the unit.
On restart it adopts the VAP it created last time rather than cloning a second
one.
.It
.Sy Nothing published an association-complete signal .
net80211 reports the link UP at
.Em association ,
which is
.Em before
the WPA 4-way handshake.
.Xr ipconfigd 8
would fire DHCP onto an unauthenticated port, have every packet dropped, burn
its ~28-second retransmit ladder, and then never retry \(em because the link is
.Em already
Active, so no new event ever arrives.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
therefore publishes
.Ql State:/Network/Interface/<if>/AirPort
carrying
.Ql Authenticated , SSID , BSSID , RSSI , Channel ,
and
.Ql Security .
.Xr ipconfigd 8
requires
.Ql Link{Active}
.Sy and
.Ql AirPort{Authenticated}
before it will send a DHCPDISCOVER.
An interface with
.Em no
AirPort key is treated as ready, which is what keeps every wired NIC behaving
exactly as it did before.
.Sh RADIOS
net80211 is
.Pa Wlan.kext ,
loaded with the first Wi-Fi driver kext that matches hardware.
It publishes each radio in the IORegistry as an
.Ql IO80211Controller
entry, named after the radio
.Pq Ql iwlwifi0 ,
once the driver has attached it, and retires the entry when the radio goes
away: its driver kext is unloaded or a USB radio is unplugged.
.Nm
follows that class with
.Fn IOServiceAddMatchingNotification ,
first-match and terminated, as Apple's
.Ql wifid
follows
.Ql IO80211Controller .
When an entry appears,
.Nm
clones the VAP and starts
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
for every radio in
.Va net.wlan.devices
it does not manage yet.
When one goes, it removes the AirPort key, stops the supplicant and forgets the
interface; the VAP is already gone.
With no radio,
.Nm
logs one line and blocks with no timer.
.Pp
On a kernel without
.Pa /dev/ioregistry ,
it rescans
.Va net.wlan.devices
every 2 seconds instead.
.Sh ARCHITECTURE
.Bd -literal -offset indent
wland ──(wpa_ctrl socket)──▶ stock wpa_supplicant (from base)
      ──(SCDynamicStore)───▶ configd  ──▶ ipconfigd's DHCP gate
      ──(SCPreferences)────▶ known networks
      ──(MIG org.nextbsd.wlan)──▶ wlan(8) ──▶ Gershwin
.Ed
.Pp
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
is
.Sy stock ,
from FreeBSD base: not vendored, not patched, not taught Mach, and not the
.Pa security/wpa_supplicant
port.
It speaks net80211 ioctls downward and a UNIX control socket upward, and does
not know configd exists.
All Mach knowledge lives in
.Nm .
Keeping the supplicant stock means a security fix is a base rebuild rather than
a merge against local patches forever.
.Pp
.Nm
spawns
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
itself \(em
.Xr launchd 8
cannot, because it needs
.Ql -i wlan0
and
.Li wlan0
does not exist until
.Nm
creates it.
It is spawned with an
.Sy empty
configuration and
.Ql update_config=0 ,
and every network is injected at runtime over the control socket.
.Pp
This matters:
.Nm
is the
.Sy sole author
of
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8 Ns 's
network blocks.
If the configuration file also carried SSIDs, the supplicant's own autojoin and
.Nm Ns 's
autojoin would both be choosing networks \(em two brains, fighting.
That is the classic NetworkManager failure mode, and it produces exactly the
behaviour users hate: the machine keeps rejoining the wrong network and nothing
you click stops it.
.Sh AUTOJOIN
.Nm
picks the strongest remembered, autojoin-enabled network currently in range.
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
cannot do this: it offers only a
.Ql priority
integer, which cannot express
.Dq prefer whichever of my known networks I can actually hear best right now .
.Sh KNOWN NETWORKS AND PASSPHRASE STORAGE
Remembered networks live in a root-owned
.Pa preferences.plist
under
.Pa /Local/Library/Preferences/SystemConfiguration ,
written through SCPreferences (atomic commit and locking come free).
.Pp
.Sy Passphrases are stored in plaintext .
This is not a design preference.
NextBSD has no keychain \(em it is not started and not planned \(em so WLAN
passphrases are plaintext on disk whichever path is taken.
The only real choice is
.Em which
plaintext file, and this one keeps
.Nm
the sole author of the supplicant's network blocks.
The file is mode 0600 and root-owned.
If a keychain lands, this is the one thing that changes.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/Local/Library/Preferences/SystemConfiguration/org.nextbsd.wland.plist" -compact
.It Pa /usr/sbin/wland
The daemon.
.It Pa /dev/ioregistry
The in-kernel IORegistry, where radios appear as
.Ql IO80211Controller .
.It Pa /System/Library/LaunchDaemons/org.nextbsd.wland.plist
.Xr launchd 8
job.
.It Pa /var/log/wland.stderr
Log.
.It Pa /var/run/wland/wpa-<if>.conf
The deliberately empty
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
config.
.Sy Never add networks here .
.It Pa /var/run/wpa_supplicant/<if>
The supplicant's control socket.
.It Pa /Local/Library/Preferences/SystemConfiguration/org.nextbsd.wland.plist
Known networks (plaintext passphrases).
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr configd 8 ,
.Xr ioreg 8 ,
.Xr ipconfigd 8 ,
.Xr launchd 8 ,
.Xr wlan 8 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
.Pp
.Lk https://pkgdemon.github.io/nextbsd-wlan-plan.html "The NextBSD WLAN plan"
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in NextBSD in 2026.
It is a NextBSD original.
Apple's counterpart,
.Ql wifid ,
is closed source; the only piece Apple ever published
.Pq Ql eapolclient
performs the EAP exchange and nothing else \(em no scanning, no association, no
4-way handshake \(em so there was no seed to build from.
.Sh CAVEATS
On a machine with no Wi-Fi hardware,
.Pa Wlan.kext
is never loaded,
.Va net.wlan.devices
does not exist, and
.Nm
waits for a radio that does not come.
.Pp
WPA-Enterprise (802.1X) is not implemented.
It would come from
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8 Ns 's
own EAP stack, or not at all.
